Z||000024||Doni Hagan||08-26-2001||10:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>I'm planning on attending Fierorama 2001 with my wife.  it is close to my wedding anniversary and was wondering if there is anywhere near there that is a "NICE" place to stay? (you know what I mean  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) Any suggestions would be helpful!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How much are you thinking to spend and would you consider staying in the city? There are some excellent hotels in town I can recommend (I put clients/accounts up in some of them for business trips) and Oak Brook isn't particularly difficult to get to from midtown (just out the Ike X-way to I-88 South.) <P>E-mail me <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000025||Archie||08-26-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>I need to find a cheaper motel than that one.  $70 is too much money for me.  I still need something close and decent (no roach motels!). <P>Oreif--Please send me the name of that other motel.  I can't find your email.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>IMHO, the motels in that area are on the high priced side. You can go 10 minutes North or South from there and be in nice places that are half that price.<P>I put people up about 1 mile from my Condo at the Best Western in Arl.Hts. at like $40.... that's only 10 minutes from the show.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000026||Oreif||08-26-2001||11:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>I need to find a cheaper motel than that one.  $70 is too much money for me.  I still need something close and decent (no roach motels!). <P>Oreif--Please send me the name of that other motel.  I can't find your email.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Email Sent.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000027||Archie||08-26-2001||11:17 PM||||Ok, this show is only 2 weeks away now.... & we are pulling out all the stops to get our best turnout ever.<P>Among attractions is the NIFE raffle car will be given away at this show. All the tickets have been sold and you don't need to be present to win, BUT just imagine winning this thing and being there to accept it. Usually the car is given away as the last thing at the show & if you win You'll be able to head home knowing that everyone else hates you.<P>We also will be raffling off a $500 value "Warber" hood see pictures below. I am donating this item and all the funds raised will go into the NIFE treasury for future Fiero Fun. Please note that shipping and installation are not included.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/W-hood1.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/W-hood2.jpg">  <P>Typically this show draws 120 to 130 Fieros. The last couple of years' we've had a few sprinkles or we would have had 150 cars show up. This year, the weather will be perfect, you can count on it.<P>You wanna see some V-8 Fieros?.... last year we had 14 or more of them. Wanna see all kinds and shapes of Fieros and their owners?... think of it..... 150 Fieros all in one place with a McDonalds next door, what else could you ask for?<P>Just in case you haven't heard, FieroRama is "In Honor of the Daily Driven Fiero" & The Fiero classes are based on MILEAGE, not just overall condition! Us guys that drive our cars a lot actually have a chance to win something at this show.<P>Be there or be square.<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 08-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000028||Fiero5||08-26-2001||11:43 PM||||I wonder how far the show grounds are from New Hampshire?<BR>It would be cool to go to that show, but I don't know if I could get too many days off for a loong trip.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Glowing_Fiero9_sig.jpg">          <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||5
