Z||000030||Standard||08-27-2001||04:24 AM||||Well, I registered.  For some reason I'm scheduled to work saturday the 7th from 10-3, which I'm sure is a mistake but oh well.  Even if I have to stay there till 6 I decided I'm gonna go anyways.  <P>ok, just made reservations at the motel 6 in villa park, about a mile away from the show.  55 bucks for a night.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000031||FieroLT1||08-27-2001||11:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jch82:<BR><B>I hope to be there with my 85GT. I wonder if there is a "work in progress" class...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Josh   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah! That class saved me at the Dells!<BR>Got me my first Trophy ever.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>Last year I was hoping to be the only LT1 powered Fiero at Fierorama. But I wasn't.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Not that the other guy won anything either.<BR>Custom class is though!<BR>Maybe this year will come home with some hardware.<P><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
