Z||000042||MooCow||08-30-2001||01:42 AM||||Hey Im going to go.  Hopefully my one sail window will be on by then since it decided to snap in half and fly off.<BR>Haze I promise this time I will talk to you since I didnt in El Paso.<BR>So since there is going to be lots of V8 Fiero's there anyone want to give me a ride in one&gt;?&gt;?  I'll give you a ride in my car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> OOOOOO  I can't wait to actually meet more of you.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||10
Z||000043||Oreif||08-30-2001||02:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85ZainoGT:<BR><B>ok, so what EXACTLY is Fierorama?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fierorama is a large local Fiero show hosted by the Northern Illinois Fiero Enthusiasts.<BR>The difference between this and other car shows is our club honors the "Daily Driver" cars. It doesn't have to be a "show car". Your not judged on how clean the car is but the overall condition of the car as used as a daily driver. The "Show Cars" and "trailer queens" are in a "Display class" and are not judged. We plan on having over 150 Fiero's from many of the mid-west states.||||reg||1
Z||000044||MinnGreenGT||08-30-2001||10:23 AM||||I can't wait... haven't been to a real show in quite some time.  Experiencing withdrawl!  I've got 110k miles on my GT and it is my daily driver (and shows the general wear of it).  When there, everyone be sure to identify themselves by their names here also- I'm going to print a sign to go next to my car (similiar to my sig).<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
