Z||000053||TI_3VOM||09-02-2001||11:39 PM||||Roy,<BR>   We got all the rain Thursday night. The weather forecast called for some rain, but apparently no one foresaw the monsoon we recieved. The chain of events that led to the downpour was actually freakey! The cold front that moved in from the northwest (which brought in the rain that was forcast) merged/collided with the moisture that was being pushed out of northwest Indiana by all the heat there. All this erupted over the north part of Chicago. If you were to draw it out on a map, the parts of the heaviest rain fall would start around O'Hare, and pretty much follow I-90 all the way into downtown. Almost like mama nature was trying to show us something.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000054||TI_3VOM||09-02-2001||11:39 PM||||Roy,<BR>   We got all the rain Thursday night. The weather forecast called for some rain, but apparently no one foresaw the monsoon we recieved. The chain of events that led to the downpour was actually freakey! The cold front that moved in from the northwest (which brought in the rain that was forcast) merged/collided with the moisture that was being pushed out of northwest Indiana by all the heat there. All this erupted over the north part of Chicago. If you were to draw it out on a map, the parts of the heaviest rain fall would start around O'Hare, and pretty much follow I-90 all the way into downtown. Almost like mama nature was trying to show us something.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||9
